Upstream fix for the per-frame sync_file descriptor leak, backported to v7.349.0.

Original: libplacebo commit c93aa134ab62365ce1177efff99b8e1e66a818e7
          "opengl/util: fix sync object leak" (moi15moi, 2026-02-18)
          Fixes mpv-player/mpv#12708, mpv-android/mpv-android#977

Why it matters here
-------------------
`gl_poll_callbacks()` pops a callback and, on the SUCCESS path, never deletes the
`GLsync` it waited on.  Mesa backs GL sync objects with kernel fences, so each
leaked `GLsync` holds an open `sync_file` descriptor.  mpv registers a poll
callback per rendered frame, so the descriptor count grows ~1/draw call and the
frontend dies of `OSError: [Errno 24] Too many open files` after ~27s of video.

The `GL_WAIT_FAILED` branch already deletes its sync; only the success path — the
one taken every frame — leaks.  Applied to v7.349.0, which is what Debian Trixie
and Raspberry Pi OS ship (`libplacebo349 7.349.0-3`); v7.360.1 already has it.

--- a/src/opengl/utils.c
+++ b/src/opengl/utils.c
@@ -47,6 +47,7 @@ void gl_poll_callbacks(pl_gpu gpu)
         switch (res) {
         case GL_ALREADY_SIGNALED:
         case GL_CONDITION_SATISFIED:
             PL_ARRAY_REMOVE_AT(p->callbacks, 0);
+            gl->DeleteSync(cb.sync);
             cb.callback(cb.priv);
             continue;
 
